"B8Script timing check: how long n? waits. Time each step with a watch,";
"and press no keys while it runs. Steps 1 and 3 should take a second.";
"Under CP/M, n? is timed by counting keyboard checks (BDOS 6 calls), and";
"how long one takes depends on the BIOS. The CP/M builds count 4 checks";
"a millisecond, right for an RC2014 with RomWBW and ZPM3. If step 1 takes";
"T seconds on your machine, use 4 / T instead (1 to 255): patch it into";
"the .COM at the place testing/patchinfo.py prints. A generic build counts";
"MSLOOP checks: set MSLOOP to MSLOOP / T and rebuild.";
"B8Script timing check. Time each step with a watch, and press no keys while it runs./M/J"$
"Press a key for step 1: 10 x 100? (should take 1 second)/M/J"$ 0?;
10n! 1( 100?; n@1-:n! ) "done/M/J"$
"Press a key for step 2: 1000 x 1? (1 second, and a little more: the loop's own time)/M/J"$ 0?;
1000n! 1( 1?; n@1-:n! ) "done/M/J"$
"Press a key for step 3: 1 x 1000? (should take 1 second)/M/J"$ 0?;
1000?; "done/M/J"$
"Press a key for step 4: an empty loop, 10000 times (no timing: just how fast the machine is)/M/J"$ 0?;
10000n! 1( n@1-:n! ) "done/M/J"$
